\section{Introduction}
The Trichological Cycle Engine (TCE) is a sovereign autonomous
biological simulation architecture designed to model the complete
hair-follicle lifecycle under nominal, stressed, and stochastic
conditions. This laboratory manual provides a multi-experiment
framework for evaluating vitality dynamics, phase transitions,
Lyapunov stability, stress resilience, and sovereign kernel recovery.

%-----------------------------------------------------------
\section{System Overview}
The governing vitality equation is:
\begin{equation}
\frac{dF}{dt}
= \alpha^\star \mathbb{I}(\sigma=A)
- \beta^\star \mathbb{I}(\sigma=C)
- \gamma \mathbb{I}(\sigma=T)
+ \Delta S(t),
\end{equation}
with $\sigma(t)\in\{A,C,T\}$ and $\Delta S(t)$ a bounded stochastic
forcing term.

Phase transitions follow:
\begin{equation}
\sigma(t+\Delta t)=
\begin{cases}
C & \sigma(t)=A,\ F(t)\le\theta_C,\\
T & \sigma(t)=C,\ t_p\ge T_c,\\
A & \sigma(t)=T,\ F(t)\ge\theta_A.
\end{cases}
\end{equation}

